# a runtime helper no declaration names: the 128-bit formatter, demanded by any
# program that prints one. The `@` marks it as standing outside the declaration
# space, as the synthesised comparisons do. Its unit is `prelude` because of
# WHERE it goes: emitC emits it into the header, ahead of the literal pool, so
# that a need registered inside a type method is still in time.
[@prelude.fmt_128 frag=_Z_FMT_128]


# -- collections -------------------------------------------------------
# A container's natives are GENERATED: the emitter instantiates one of the
# shared .c.tmpl files per monomorphised container, so every method below comes
# out of one substitution and none has C of its own to name here. The rows say
# that the compiler supplies them -- which is what an absent row has to be able
# to deny.

